{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Progress checkpoint\n\n- F30A, herby-crude-rat, landed through Gerrit change 2168 at commit 813baac9b01524a024523a8516d563b17f395358. It received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, passed signed completion verification, and is closed.\n- Rebar-debug confirmed that the completion timeout was caused by a broad no-filter fetch across every configured origin head. The enrich drain was not the direct blocker.\n- Created sawdusty-snotty-fossa for the confirmed snapshot fetch-scope defect. Linked it discovered_from F30A and relates_to unromantic-ferny-arawana. The bug and both links are visible from the replicated tracker.\n- F30B, peppery-dire-indianabat, received a signed PASS plan review at 813baac9b01524a024523a8516d563b17f395358. Another session claimed it before this session could claim it, so this session made no F30B edits.\n- The epic currently has no claimable batch. F14, F16, and F30B remain in progress.\n- Background implementation tasks for F19A and F20 remain active. Their workers have not yet delivered status reports.\n- Refreshed origin/main to df8058c23167. The new commit adds layered tracker footprint reporting."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787545092308026001,"uuid":"149abfa8-9da0-4470-9e1d-68880f0b7a7e"}